    "content": "Chapter III: Must-Haves | PES University Handbook ✕ Chapter III The Must-Haves \"Equip yourself with the tools of critical inquiry and analytical precision.\" MATERIAL CHECK REQUIRED STATIONERY • TECHNICAL SPEC SHEET SPECIFICATION LOG NOTEBOOKS Lecture Notebooks A simple notebook is all you need to get started. At the beginning of the 1st semester, the university usually provides a 5-subject spiral notebook, which is enough for rough work or practice. Recommendations Get a larger 5-subject notebook or maintain individual books per subject for ease of understanding. Mathematics recommendation: Maintain a separate notebook as you'll be doing a lot of problems. SUBMISSION MANUAL BLUE BOOK Assignment Journals Most courses require assignments to be written in a blue book (typically priced around ₹15–20). These are readily available at the campus bookstore/Campus Mart. Shopping Tip A cheaper choice is to get blue books from outside of campus where they are available for lesser prices. If you are in a hurry, Campus Mart is always available. HARDWARE MATRIX fx-991CW Scientific Calculator A non-programmable scientific calculator is an essential tool for engineering students and will be used frequently throughout your coursework. Programmable calculators are prohibited during exams. Authorized Models Casio fx-991CW (Preferred choice, constants and more features built-in) Casio fx-991ES Plus Casio fx-82MS Tip: Seniors sell calculators in working condition at reduced, negotiable prices. READ SPEED --- WPM COMPLETED: 0%"
